> I am seeing possible perf regressions for max-throughput configs. This can impact all disagg runs using nixl backend. Should we merge regardless for correctness or should we resolve the perf regressions first, considering that the data race is quite hard to hit anyways?

@nvjullin The nixl version issue of CI has been fixed, which means we could merge now. As for the perf regressions, please investigate whether it is related to this PR (i.e., forcing syncMode = NIXL_THREAD_SYNC_STRICT).

If you think this data race issue is urgent, we could merge this PR now. And if the perf regressions turn out to be related to this PR, we could revert and find a real fix later. But if it is not that urgent, please identify the root cause of the perf regressions first; we really should not introduce a new bug while fixing one.

After offline discussion, NIXL team has filed https://github.com/ai-dynamo/nixl/pull/1811 to fix this, but meanwhile, we should use STRICT mode in SGLang for now until we upgrade to a NIXL version containing the fix.

The perf issue @nvjullin ran into seems to be a separate issue not related to this PR, so this PR should be safe to merge.

@ShangmingCai could you help us to merge this PR? thanks!

I followed what NIXL does for its own etcd
